Because cobra commands keep multiple `FlagSets` that share the underlying flags, one can end up with consistency problems when setting a `normalizeNameFunc` (if setting it after defining flags): the names in the underlying flags will be updated, but not all `FlagSets` that have references to them will know how to properly lookup the new name.

Example of bug:
```
package main

import (
	"strings"

	"github.com/spf13/cobra"
	"github.com/spf13/pflag"
)

func main() {
	cmd := &cobra.Command{}
	flagVal := false
	n := func(f *pflag.FlagSet, name string) pflag.NormalizedName {
		return pflag.NormalizedName(strings.ToUpper(name))
	}

	cmd.Flags().BoolVar(&flagVal, "flagname", true, "this is a dummy flag")
	cmd.Usage()

	cmd.SetGlobalNormalizationFunc(n)
	cmd.Usage()
}
```

Submitting two pull requests for a proposed fix:
https://github.com/spf13/cobra/pull/522
https://github.com/spf13/pflag/pull/137

